Output3Using a sliding window - O(n) Time and O(1) SpaceThe idea is to use two pointers (i and j) and a frequency array to track the count of '0', '1', and '2'. Expand the window by moving j, and when all three characters are present, shrink it from the left (i) to maintain the smallest valid substring. Print the minimum length found.Dry run for string s = "01212":Initialize i = 0, j = 0, cnt = 0, min_len = INT_MAX and freq = {0, 0, 0}For j = 0, add '0': freq = {1, 0, 0}, cnt = 1 and cnt != 3 no update, expand window.For j = 1, add '1': freq = {1, 1, 0}, cnt = 2 and cnt != 3 no update, expand window.For j = 2, add '2': freq = {1, 1, 1}, cnt = 3. Now all digits are present hence, update min_len = min(INT_MAX, 2 - 0 + 1) = 3 and remove s[i] = '0': freq = {0, 1, 1}, increment i to 1, cnt = 2For j = 3, add '1': freq = {0, 2, 1}, cnt = 2 and cnt != 3 no update, expand window.For j = 4, add '2': freq = {0, 2, 2}, cnt = 2 and cnt != 3 no update, expand window.So, final answer is min_len = 3.
